translated_text:
CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 8

Women and Children who are victims of acts of Violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
f. the right to restitution;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to obtain facilities in the judicial process; and/or j. the right to assistance.

text:
Pasal 1 I

Anak sebagai korban tindak selain mendapatkan hak-hak Kekerasan sebagaimala dimaksud dalam Pasal 8, juga mendapatkan hak khusus, sebagai berikut:
a. hak penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang; b. hak pelayanan dasar;
c. hak perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan/ataue. hak mendapatkal kebebasan.

translated_text:
Article 11

Children as victims of acts of Violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 8, also receive special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development; b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or

e. the right to obtain freedom.

